{
  "id": 477178244,
  "iid": 24558,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "kerberos: Fix compilation with Heimdal for recent changes",
  "description": "Update the Heimdal path for the read_keytab_file commit\n91eef8bb37c36d6dc6aa31521b86dc4919624d7a\n\nInstead of having two nearly identical keytab_file_read\nfunctions, have ifdefs for the small differnces. Some of\nthe defines are taken from Samba's krb5_samba.h\n\nUse standard function krb5_unparse_name instead of manually\naccessing struct members (the output is the same). Call\nwmem_strbuf_finalize instead of just wmem_strbuf_get_str\nwhen done with the wmem_strbuf.\n\nAlso fix an issue where the new key's length member was being\nset to the full length from the copied key even though the array\nwas limited to the max length. (This should not be a problem in\npractice but is safer.)\n\nAlso update for the -Wpointer-sign change.\n\nWe probably will deprecated Heimdal Kerberos, but this gets\nthe code building again on the master branch. (4.6 and earlier\nare ok.) Tested with Debian stable's heimdal-dev.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
